1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-5--5a-writing-comfort","kind":"phase-article","route":"/roadmap/phase-5/5a-writing-comfort","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-5/5a-writing-comfort","sourceHash":"6cbcf404e238875e651b193183d6079f210ad4d44786fa1f041973475113c397","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:58.015Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"5A — Writing Comfort","zh":"5A——写作适应"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"what-youre-doing","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What You're Doing","zh":"你正在做什么"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You can speak the language, but you haven't <em>really</em> written in it. Before you can use writing as a tool to improve your accuracy (which it's fantastic for), you need to get comfortable with the physical and mental act of writing: the keyboard layout (or handwriting system), the spelling conventions, and the process of putting your thoughts into text.","zh":"你已经可以说这门语言，但还没有<em>真正</em>用它写过东西。在你能够把写作当作提高准确性的工具之前（写作对此非常有效），你需要先适应写作这一身体和心理活动：键盘布局（或书写系统）、拼写规范，以及把想法转化为文字的过程。"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This sub-phase isn't about writing <strong>well</strong>. It's about writing <em>at all</em>. Quantity over quality. Get words on the page and build up the muscle memory and mental habits that make writing feel natural.","zh":"这个子阶段的重点不是写得<strong>好</strong>，而是<em>写出来</em>。数量优先于质量。把文字写在纸面上，逐步建立肌肉记忆和心理习惯，让写作变得自然。"}},{"id":"whats-new","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What's New","zh":"有什么新内容"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Unassisted Writing</strong> — Writing without any tools (except maybe a keyboard or pencil... Those aren't the tools we mean). No dictionary, no grammar checker, no help. Just you and your thoughts. The goal here is fluency, not accuracy. Write fast, write messy, don't worry about mistakes. Journal entries, stream-of-consciousness writing, descriptions of your day — anything goes. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/unassisted-writing\">Unassisted Writing</a>","zh":"<strong>无辅助写作</strong>——不借助任何工具写作（键盘或铅笔或许算，但我们指的不是这些）。不用词典，不用语法检查器，也不寻求帮助。只有你和你的想法。这里的目标是流利，而不是准确。写快一点，写得潦草一点，不必担心错误。日记、意识流写作、描述一天的经历——什么都可以。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/unassisted-writing\">无辅助写作</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Assisted Writing</strong> — Writing with tools available: a dictionary, a grammar reference, or an AI chatbot to check your sentences. The goal is to stretch yourself — look up words you don't know how to write, double-check grammar when you're unsure, and generally use every tool at your disposal to produce text that's better than what you could write unaided. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/assisted-writing\">Assisted Writing</a>","zh":"<strong>辅助写作</strong>——使用可用工具进行写作：词典、语法参考资料，或用于检查句子的 AI 聊天机器人。目标是挑战自己——查找不会拼写的词，不确定时再次确认语法，并充分利用手头的工具，写出比完全不借助帮助时更好的文本。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/assisted-writing\">辅助写作</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Typing Practice</strong> — If your target language uses a different keyboard layout or script, you'll need dedicated practice to build typing speed. Even if the script is the same, the letter combinations are different, and your fingers need to learn them. Aim for at least 25 words per minute before moving on. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/typing-practice\">Typing Practice</a>","zh":"<strong>打字练习</strong>——如果你的目标语言使用不同的键盘布局或文字系统，就需要专门练习来提高打字速度。即使文字系统相同，字母组合也不同，你的手指需要熟悉这些组合。在继续下一步之前，目标是达到至少每分钟 25 个词。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/typing-practice\">打字练习</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<em>Note: Unless you specifically need handwriting for practical purposes (or really really want to work on it), then you should probably work on it later (in Phase 6 or 7). It's needlessly slow for this phase.</em>","zh":"<em>注意：除非你出于实际需要必须练习手写（或者真的非常想练），否则最好晚些时候再练（第 6 或第 7 阶段）。在这个阶段，手写会不必要地拖慢进度。</em>"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Topic Writing</strong> — Writing over and over about a specific subject, which forces you to repeatedly use vocabulary and structures and build up competence. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/topic-writing\">Topic Writing</a>","zh":"<strong>主题写作</strong>——反复围绕特定主题写作，迫使你重复使用词汇和语言结构，并逐步建立能力。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/topic-writing\">主题写作</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You should also continue speaking — monologuing or conversation practice — to maintain what you built in Phase 4. Don't let your speaking skills atrophy while you develop writing!","zh":"你也应该继续练习口语——进行独白或对话练习——以保持第 4 阶段建立的能力。不要在培养写作能力的同时，让口语能力退化！"}},{"id":"your-routine","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Your Routine","zh":"你的日常安排"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Output dominates, with writing as the main focus: <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">The Pillars of Language Learning</a>","zh":"输出占主导地位，写作是主要重点：<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">语言学习的支柱</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Priming:</strong> 10%","zh":"<strong>准备：</strong>10%"},{"en":"<strong>Interactive Immersion:</strong> 20%","zh":"<strong>互动沉浸：</strong>20%"},{"en":"<strong>Freeflow Immersion:</strong> 20%","zh":"<strong>自由流沉浸：</strong>20%"},{"en":"<strong>Output:</strong> 50%","zh":"<strong>输出：</strong>50%"}]},{"id":"sample-daily-schedule","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Sample Daily Schedule","zh":"每日安排示例"}},{"id":"segment-0015","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Vocab study: 10 mins","zh":"词汇学习：10 分钟"},{"en":"Interactive Reading: 20 mins","zh":"互动阅读：20 分钟"},{"en":"Freeflow Listening: 20 mins","zh":"自由流听力：20 分钟"},{"en":"Typing Practice: 10 mins","zh":"打字练习：10 分钟"},{"en":"Assisted Writing: 30 mins","zh":"辅助写作：30 分钟"},{"en":"Monologuing: 10 mins","zh":"独白练习：10 分钟"}]},{"id":"when-to-move-on","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Move On","zh":"何时进入下一阶段"}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Move to 5B when you:","zh":"满足以下条件后进入 5B："}},{"id":"segment-0018","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Have written at least 5000 words total (uncorrected)","zh":"累计写作至少 5000 个词（未经纠正）"},{"en":"Can write an understandable text of 500+ words with the help of a dictionary","zh":"借助词典，能够写出一篇 500 个词以上且易于理解的文章"},{"en":"Can type at 25+ words per minute (if applicable)","zh":"能够达到每分钟 25 个词以上的打字速度（如适用）"}]}],"cards":[]}}]
